# The demos that render from the compiled-in core alone — no font tree, no packages on disk.
#
# Everything reachable without an installation is here: the engine's own typesetting, mathematics
# (which needs no package), the base and document packages, drop caps, page geometry and
# arrangement, and the two barcode symbologies. Every other demo names a catalogue face or a
# package that lives on
# disk, and must fail with a diagnostic saying so rather than rendering something wrong.
#
# Regenerate with tools/render-corpus.sh and read the diff before accepting it: a demo LEAVING
# this file means an unconfigured texish can do less than it used to.
#
# Lines starting with # are ignored. Keep the rest sorted.
datamatrix-demo
document-demo
dropcap-demo
four-up-dummy
geometry-demo
math-demo
qr-demo
texish-demo
